      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to the [[credential-scoping]] page, the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned Ingest and Query agent child processes immediately before they start**, not held in the Hub\u0027s own process environment. \n\nSpecifically, the page says:\n\n\u003E \u0022a local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it only into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts.\u0022\n\nThe same approach is used for the Query agent\u2014it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time. This scoping ensures that a compromised Hub process cannot leak the API key by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key only exists within the short-lived child processes that actually call the Anthropic API.",
